["<aside class=\"callout why\" role=\"note\"><div class=\"callout-t\">Why it matters</div><p>In coast timber you rarely see a deer first. It smells, hears or sees you. Know its senses and its day, and the odds turn.</p></aside><figure class=\"diagram\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" viewBox=\"0 0 400 325\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"A day curve: deer movement peaks near dawn and dusk, lower at midday and at night, but deer can move any time. Legal hunting hours run from 1 hour before sunrise to 1 hour after sunset.\">\n<rect width=\"400\" height=\"325\" fill=\"#EEF1EA\"/>\n<text x=\"200\" y=\"28\" font-size=\"18\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#1F3D2B\">The deer day</text>\n<rect x=\"14\" y=\"60\" width=\"372\" height=\"120\" rx=\"8\" fill=\"#ffffff\" stroke=\"#1F3D2B\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><path d=\"M24 160 C60 160 70 80 96 80 C122 80 132 150 170 150 C220 150 230 150 260 150 C290 150 300 80 322 80 C346 80 356 160 376 160\" fill=\"#cfe0c3\" stroke=\"#1F3D2B\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><text x=\"96\" y=\"74\" font-size=\"15\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#1F3D2B\">dawn</text><text x=\"322\" y=\"74\" font-size=\"15\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#1F3D2B\">dusk</text><text x=\"24\" y=\"200\" font-size=\"14\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-weight=\"normal\" fill=\"#17201A\">night</text><text x=\"200\" y=\"200\" font-size=\"14\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"normal\" fill=\"#17201A\">midday</text><text x=\"376\" y=\"200\" font-size=\"14\" text-anchor=\"end\" font-weight=\"normal\" fill=\"#17201A\">night</text><rect x=\"60\" y=\"214\" width=\"300\" height=\"22\" rx=\"4\" fill=\"#FF6A13\" stroke=\"none\" stroke-width=\"0\"/><text x=\"210\" y=\"230\" font-size=\"14\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#ffffff\">Legal hours</text><text x=\"200\" y=\"262\" font-size=\"14\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"normal\" fill=\"#17201A\">1 hour before sunrise to</text><text x=\"200\" y=\"282\" font-size=\"14\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"normal\" fill=\"#17201A\">1 hour after sunset (99%)</text><text x=\"200\" y=\"310\" font-size=\"15\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#1F3D2B\">Most active near dawn and dusk (80%)</text>\n</svg>\n</figure><ul><li>Most active near dawn and dusk; can move any time <span class=\"cert c-mid\" title=\"Certainty\">80%</span>.</li><li>Legal hours: 1 hour before sunrise to 1 hour after sunset <span class=\"cert c-hi\" title=\"Certainty\">99%</span>.</li></ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>More: the day in detail</summary><aside class=\"callout warn\" role=\"note\"><div class=\"callout-t\">Warning</div><p>Study aid only. The official regulations are the law.</p></aside><ul><li>Deer \"are most active near dawn and dusk\" and \"may be active at any time of day\" (80%, WDFW, Washington Department of Fish and Wildlife).</li><li>About half a deer's time is spent in 5 to 10% of its home range (90%, Nyberg and Janz 1990, Vancouver Island data).</li><li>Favourite bedding sites may be used daily for several weeks, and again the next year <span class=\"cert c-mid\" title=\"Certainty\">90%</span>.</li><li>No hunting game except migratory birds from 1 hour after sunset to 1 hour before sunrise (99%, page 11, item 38). The app shows sunrise and sunset for your plan (Tip: check the night before).</li><li>In the November rut, bucks also move in daylight (80%, <a href=\"#/s/local-harrison-deer\">Your Harrison deer hunt</a>). Chapter 4.</li></ul></details>","<figure class=\"diagram\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" viewBox=\"0 0 400 325\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"A hunter looks at thick young conifers 60 m away. A deer stands behind them, mostly hidden. Good security cover hides about 90% of a deer at 60 m. Look for parts, not a whole deer.\">\n<rect width=\"400\" height=\"325\" fill=\"#EEF1EA\"/>\n<text x=\"200\" y=\"28\" font-size=\"18\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#1F3D2B\">Hidden in plain sight</text>\n<rect x=\"14\" y=\"46\" width=\"372\" height=\"190\" rx=\"10\" fill=\"#ffffff\" stroke=\"#1F3D2B\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><circle cx=\"54\" cy=\"150\" r=\"10\" fill=\"#17201A\"/><rect x=\"46\" y=\"160\" width=\"16\" height=\"40\" fill=\"#17201A\"/><line x1=\"70\" y1=\"214\" x2=\"300\" y2=\"214\" stroke=\"#1F3D2B\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><text x=\"185\" y=\"206\" font-size=\"15\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#1F3D2B\">60 m (66 yd)</text><ellipse cx=\"320\" cy=\"168\" rx=\"34\" ry=\"16\" fill=\"#8b5a2b\"/><ellipse cx=\"350\" cy=\"146\" rx=\"10\" ry=\"7\" fill=\"#8b5a2b\"/><path d=\"M276 210 L288 120 L300 210 Z\" fill=\"#8a9a6b\" stroke=\"#1F3D2B\" stroke-width=\"1\"/><path d=\"M296 210 L308 120 L320 210 Z\" fill=\"#8a9a6b\" stroke=\"#1F3D2B\" stroke-width=\"1\"/><path d=\"M316 210 L328 120 L340 210 Z\" fill=\"#8a9a6b\" stroke=\"#1F3D2B\" stroke-width=\"1\"/><path d=\"M336 210 L348 120 L360 210 Z\" fill=\"#8a9a6b\" stroke=\"#1F3D2B\" stroke-width=\"1\"/><path d=\"M356 210 L368 120 L380 210 Z\" fill=\"#8a9a6b\" stroke=\"#1F3D2B\" stroke-width=\"1\"/><text x=\"200\" y=\"264\" font-size=\"15\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#17201A\">Good cover hides 90% of a deer at 60 m</text><text x=\"200\" y=\"286\" font-size=\"14\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"normal\" fill=\"#17201A\">(mule deer research, 85%)</text><text x=\"200\" y=\"310\" font-size=\"15\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#FF6A13\">Look for parts, not a whole deer (Tip)</text>\n</svg>\n</figure><ul><li>Coast deer like cover close by, even when they do not need it <span class=\"cert c-mid\" title=\"Certainty\">90%</span>.</li></ul><ul><li>Beds: flattened plants about 0.9 to 1.2 m long <span class=\"cert c-mid\" title=\"Certainty\">80%</span>.</li></ul>","<div class=\"gallery\"><figure class=\"photo\"><img src=\"photos/g-bt-bedded.jpg\" alt=\"Bedded: only the head and ears show.\" loading=\"lazy\"><figcaption>Bedded: only the head and ears show. <span class=\"credit\">Photo: Buiobuione, CC BY-SA 4.0, <a href=\"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Black-tailed_deer_-_Odocoileus_hemionus_columbianus_-_05.jpg\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">source</a></span></figcaption></figure></div><details class=\"more\"><summary>More: cover in detail</summary><ul><li>Deer prefer cover close by, even when they do not need it; their use of clearcuts falls with distance from forest cover (90%, Nyberg and Janz 1990).</li><li>Mule deer research: the best security cover hides about 90% of a deer at 60 m or less (85%, cited in Nyberg and Janz).</li><li>Coast security cover: old growth with a patchy young conifer understorey, dense young stands with live branches to the ground, thickets of young cedar or hemlock <span class=\"cert c-mid\" title=\"Certainty\">90%</span>.</li><li>Deer are sometimes found bedded in recent clearcuts with plants only 1.5 to 2 m tall <span class=\"cert c-mid\" title=\"Certainty\">90%</span>.</li><li>A bed: flattened plants about 3 to 4 feet long and 2 to 3 feet wide (0.9 to 1.2 m by 0.6 to 0.9 m) (80%, WDFW).</li><li>Thermal cover: in summer deer start to pant at about 27°C; in winter a yearling's comfort zone runs from about minus 6°C to 18°C in still air <span class=\"cert c-mid\" title=\"Certainty\">90%</span>.</li><li>Full lesson: <a href=\"#/s/bedding-cover\">Bedding, terrain and thermal cover</a>.</li></ul></details>","<figure class=\"diagram\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" viewBox=\"0 0 400 300\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"Three cards. Nose: keep the wind in your face, play the thermals, check the wind every 10 minutes. Ears: step, stop, step; soft fabric; tape metal; whisper or use hand signs. Eyes: move only when its head is down; stay off the skyline.\">\n<rect width=\"400\" height=\"300\" fill=\"#fffaf0\"/>\n<text x=\"200\" y=\"22\" font-size=\"17\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"bold\">Beat each sense</text><rect x=\"14\" y=\"44\" width=\"118\" height=\"232\" rx=\"10\" fill=\"#fffaf0\" stroke=\"#e8590c\" stroke-width=\"3\"/><rect x=\"14\" y=\"44\" width=\"118\" height=\"40\" rx=\"10\" fill=\"#e8590c\"/><text x=\"73\" y=\"71\" font-size=\"18\" fill=\"#fffaf0\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"bold\">Nose</text><text x=\"73\" y=\"112\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Wind in your face</text><text x=\"73\" y=\"148\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Play thermals</text><text x=\"73\" y=\"184\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Check every</text><text x=\"73\" y=\"220\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"middle\">10 minutes</text><rect x=\"142\" y=\"44\" width=\"118\" height=\"232\" rx=\"10\" fill=\"#fffaf0\" stroke=\"#4a7fb0\" stroke-width=\"3\"/><rect x=\"142\" y=\"44\" width=\"118\" height=\"40\" rx=\"10\" fill=\"#4a7fb0\"/><text x=\"201\" y=\"71\" font-size=\"18\" fill=\"#fffaf0\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"bold\">Ears</text><text x=\"201\" y=\"112\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Step, stop, step</text><text x=\"201\" y=\"148\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Soft fabric</text><text x=\"201\" y=\"184\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Tape metal</text><text x=\"201\" y=\"220\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Whisper or sign</text><rect x=\"270\" y=\"44\" width=\"118\" height=\"232\" rx=\"10\" fill=\"#fffaf0\" stroke=\"#8a9a6b\" stroke-width=\"3\"/><rect x=\"270\" y=\"44\" width=\"118\" height=\"40\" rx=\"10\" fill=\"#8a9a6b\"/><text x=\"329\" y=\"71\" font-size=\"18\" fill=\"#fffaf0\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"bold\">Eyes</text><text x=\"329\" y=\"112\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Move when its</text><text x=\"329\" y=\"148\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"middle\">head is down</text><text x=\"329\" y=\"184\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Stay off the</text><text x=\"329\" y=\"220\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"middle\">skyline</text><text x=\"200\" y=\"294\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#6b4f35\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Opinion from the facts in this chapter (Tip)</text>\n</svg>\n</figure><ul><li>Smell is the strongest sense <span class=\"cert c-mid\" title=\"Certainty\">85%</span>. Wind in your face.</li><li>Eyes catch motion; ears catch high pitched noise (80 to 85%).</li></ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>More: the senses in detail</summary><ul><li>Black tails and mule deer are one species, so the senses are the same (75%, my reading). Full detail: <a href=\"#/s/mc-mule-deer-03\">Mule deer Masterclass 3</a>.</li><li>Smell: the strongest deer sense <span class=\"cert c-mid\" title=\"Certainty\">85%</span>. \"They also have a good sense of smell\" (80%, WDFW).</li><li>Hearing: about 115 Hz to 54 kHz, best about 4 to 8 kHz: zips, Velcro, nylon, metal clicks (85%, D'Angelo and others 2007).</li><li>Sight: about 310 degrees without turning the head, poor depth, superb at motion (80%, Penn State Deer Research). \"Remain absolutely still, because deer are alert for any movement\" (80%, WDFW).</li><li>Colour: no red cone, so blaze orange looks dull to a deer <span class=\"cert c-lo\" title=\"Certainty\">75%</span>.</li><li>Glands (90%, BC deer account): metatarsal (outside of the lower leg) gives alarm scent; tarsal (inside of the hock) for recognition; interdigital (between the toes) leaves a scent trail. Black tails have smaller hock glands than mule deer (90%, Nyberg and Janz).</li></ul></details>","<figure class=\"diagram\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" viewBox=\"0 0 400 520\" font-family=\"sans-serif\">\n  <defs>\n    <marker id=\"th-arrow\" viewBox=\"0 0 10 10\" refX=\"8\" refY=\"5\" markerWidth=\"7\" markerHeight=\"7\" orient=\"auto\">\n      <path d=\"M0,0 L10,5 L0,10 Z\" fill=\"#e8590c\"/>\n    </marker>\n  </defs>\n  <rect x=\"0\" y=\"0\" width=\"400\" height=\"520\" fill=\"#fffaf0\"/>\n  <text x=\"200\" y=\"26\" font-size=\"18\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Morning: sun warms slope, air rises</text>\n  <circle cx=\"350\" cy=\"62\" r=\"16\" fill=\"#e8590c\" fill-opacity=\"0.6\" stroke=\"#e8590c\" stroke-width=\"2\"/>\n  <path d=\"M10,240 L120,200 L260,90 L300,80 L390,150 L390,240 Z\" fill=\"#8a9a6b\" stroke=\"#2f3a2b\" stroke-width=\"2\"/>\n  <path d=\"M90,190 L150,160\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#e8590c\" stroke-width=\"3\" marker-end=\"url(#th-arrow)\"/>\n  <path d=\"M160,148 L215,108\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#e8590c\" stroke-width=\"3\" marker-end=\"url(#th-arrow)\"/>\n  <path d=\"M225,96 L262,68\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#e8590c\" stroke-width=\"3\" marker-end=\"url(#th-arrow)\"/>\n  <circle cx=\"275\" cy=\"76\" r=\"9\" fill=\"#6b4f35\" stroke=\"#23261f\" stroke-width=\"2\"/>\n  <text x=\"275\" y=\"60\" font-size=\"15\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"bold\">You</text>\n  <ellipse cx=\"80\" cy=\"212\" rx=\"14\" ry=\"8\" fill=\"#6b4f35\" stroke=\"#23261f\" stroke-width=\"2\"/>\n  <text x=\"62\" y=\"186\" font-size=\"15\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"bold\">Deer</text>\n  <text x=\"200\" y=\"230\" font-size=\"15\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Be ABOVE. Scent goes up, away.</text>\n  <line x1=\"20\" y1=\"262\" x2=\"380\" y2=\"262\" stroke=\"#8a9a6b\" stroke-width=\"2\"/>\n  <text x=\"200\" y=\"292\" font-size=\"18\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Evening: slope cools, air sinks</text>\n  <circle cx=\"350\" cy=\"322\" r=\"14\" fill=\"#8a9a6b\" stroke=\"#2f3a2b\" stroke-width=\"2\"/>\n  <path d=\"M10,500 L120,460 L260,350 L300,340 L390,410 L390,500 Z\" fill=\"#8a9a6b\" stroke=\"#2f3a2b\" stroke-width=\"2\"/>\n  <path d=\"M245,352 L195,390\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#e8590c\" stroke-width=\"3\" marker-end=\"url(#th-arrow)\"/>\n  <path d=\"M185,400 L135,437\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#e8590c\" stroke-width=\"3\" marker-end=\"url(#th-arrow)\"/>\n  <path d=\"M120,450 L70,470\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#e8590c\" stroke-width=\"3\" marker-end=\"url(#th-arrow)\"/>\n  <ellipse cx=\"270\" cy=\"338\" rx=\"14\" ry=\"8\" fill=\"#6b4f35\" stroke=\"#23261f\" stroke-width=\"2\"/>\n  <text x=\"270\" y=\"320\" font-size=\"15\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"bold\">Deer</text>\n  <circle cx=\"60\" cy=\"470\" r=\"9\" fill=\"#6b4f35\" stroke=\"#23261f\" stroke-width=\"2\"/>\n  <text x=\"48\" y=\"448\" font-size=\"15\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"bold\">You</text>\n  <text x=\"250\" y=\"485\" font-size=\"15\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Be BELOW. Scent sinks, away.</text>\n</svg>\n</figure><ul><li>Morning sun: air drifts uphill. Evening: downhill <span class=\"cert c-mid\" title=\"Certainty\">80%</span>.</li></ul><ul><li>Coast timber swirls wind. Check it often (Tip).</li></ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>More: wind and rain in detail</summary><ul><li>Sun warms a slope and scent rises; evening cooling sends scent downhill (80%, <a href=\"#/s/wind-thermals\">Wind and thermals</a>).</li><li>In tall timber and creek draws the wind swirls. Carry a puffer or thread and check every few minutes (Tip).</li><li>Rain: wet ground is quiet underfoot (Tip, <a href=\"#/s/wet-forest-country\">Wet forests</a>).</li><li>Heavy rain and wind make deer harder to see and hear you; many hunters still hunt them (Tip). No study found for black tails and rain: <span class=\"verify\">VERIFY</span> before trusting any rule of thumb.</li></ul></details><aside class=\"callout rule\" role=\"note\"><div class=\"callout-t\">Grandpa's rule (wisdom, not law)</div><p>Grandpa's rule (wisdom, not law): \"In the timber you hunt with your nose second and your patience first.\"</p></aside>","<aside class=\"callout mistake\" role=\"note\"><div class=\"callout-t\">Common mistakes</div><ul><li>Walking with the wind at your back into thick cover.</li><li>Moving when the deer's head is up.</li><li>Swishing nylon rain gear in a quiet stand.</li></ul></aside><aside class=\"callout field\" role=\"note\"><div class=\"callout-t\">Do this in the field</div><p>Next scouting walk: find 3 beds. For each, stand in it and look out. What cover hides it? Which way does the wind come?</p></aside>","<ul><li>WDFW deer page <span class=\"cert c-mid\" title=\"Certainty\">80%</span>. Nyberg and Janz 1990 <span class=\"cert c-mid\" title=\"Certainty\">90%</span>. BC deer account <span class=\"cert c-mid\" title=\"Certainty\">90%</span>. Senses research via the mule deer chapter (80 to 85%). Synopsis page 11 <span class=\"cert c-hi\" title=\"Certainty\">99%</span>. Checked 2026-10-23.</li></ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>More: every source and link</summary><ul><li>Washington Department of Fish and Wildlife, <a href=\"https://wdfw.wa.gov/species-habitats/living/species-facts/deer\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Living with wildlife: deer</a>, read 2026-10-23 <span class=\"cert c-mid\" title=\"Certainty\">80%</span>.</li><li>Nyberg and Janz, editors (1990), <a href=\"https://www.for.gov.bc.ca/hfd/pubs/docs/srs/Srs05.htm\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">\"Deer and Elk Habitats in Coastal Forests of Southern British Columbia\"</a>, pages 34, 45 to 46, 53, read directly from page images 2026-10-23 <span class=\"cert c-mid\" title=\"Certainty\">90%</span>.</li><li>BC Ministry of Environment, Lands and Parks (2000), <a href=\"https://www.env.gov.bc.ca/wld/documents/muledeer.pdf\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">\"Mule and Black-tailed Deer in British Columbia\"</a>, read directly <span class=\"cert c-mid\" title=\"Certainty\">90%</span>.</li><li>Senses sources as listed in <a href=\"#/s/mc-mule-deer-03\">Mule deer Masterclass 3</a>: Penn State Deer Research, D'Angelo and others 2007, Jacobs and others 1994 (80 to 85%).</li><li>BC Hunting and Trapping Regulations Synopsis 2026 to 2028, page 11, item 38, via <a href=\"#/s/local-harrison-deer\">Your Harrison deer hunt</a> <span class=\"cert c-hi\" title=\"Certainty\">99%</span>.</li></ul></details>"]